<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa mohair prices higher at first summer sale.</title>
<headline>S.Africa mohair prices higher at first summer sale.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African mohair prices for the first summer sale were higher, the Mohair Board</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>Of the 975 bales offered 42 percent was sold.</p>
<p>Approximate prices in South African cents a kg:</p>
<p>Adults	  long	 1303-2580	(2350-3000)</p>
<p>		  medium     2210-2210	(2200-2200)</p>
<p>		  short	2052-2600	(2000-2050)</p>
<p>Young Goats   long	 2700-5000	(2400-3992)</p>
<p>		  medium	   -	    (2200-2300)</p>
<p>		  short	    -	    (2050-2050)</p>
<p>Fine Kids     long	 5000-10000     (2800-8000)</p>
<p>		  medium     4300-7000	(2700-3300)</p>
<p>		  short	2700-4800	(2800-3202)</p>
<p>The second sale of the season is scheduled for March 11, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
